<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-Nov 1996 aluminium exports 2.38 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-Nov 1996 aluminium exports 2.38 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia exported 2.38 million tonnes of primary aluminium to countries outside the Commonwealth of Independent States over the first 11 months of 1996, State Statistics Committee data showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The figure, as reported by Interfax news agency, represented an 18 percent increase over year-ago levels.</p>
<p>The committee's figures showed nickel exports rose six percent year-on-year in the first 11 months of 1996 to 146,000 tonnes, while exports of copper climbed 14 percent to 476,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The committee released the following data for metals exports</p>
<p>-		RUSSIAN NON-CIS EXPORTS OF NON-FERROUS METALS</p>
<p>		    Jan-Nov 1996   Jan-Nov 1995   pct change</p>
<p>		     (tonnes)	 (tonnes)	  yr/yr</p>
<p> Aluminium	 2,375,200	2,007,300	  +18</p>
<p> Copper		476,100	  416,500	  +14</p>
<p> Nickel		146,100	  137,500	   +6</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
